			"Message": "fix(Sky): Consolidate bridge event routing, fix SCM registration race, and correct completion text handling\n\nSeveral critical gaps in the Sky bridge layer have been addressed to ensure reliable IPC between the UI and Mountain, and correct behavior for extension-host features.\n\nIn InstallEditorOperations, consolidate two separate subscriptions on `onDidChangeActiveCodeEditor` into a single handler. The previous dual-listener setup caused the `sky:editor:activeChanged` IPC to fire twice on every editor switch, doubling downstream load and causing unbounded listener accumulation when selection listeners were not properly disposed.\n\nIn InstallScm, resolve a race condition where `sky://scm/registerGroup` events arriving too early would permanently lose SCM groups due to missing Emitter/URI services. Introduce a `TryRegisterScmGroupWithRetry` mechanism with exponential backoff to guarantee group registration. Additionally, correct the `splice` call signature to pass the resources array directly, as the custom wrapper handles the internal spread, preventing \"iterable\" errors on empty states.\n\nIn InstallInlineCompletions, fix corruption in non-snippet completions. The logic previously wrapped all text in `{ snippet }`, causing literal `$` and `\\` characters to be interpreted as snippet syntax. Now, text is only wrapped when `isSnippet` is explicitly true.\n\nIn InstallDeadChannelListeners, InstallEditorAndOutput, and InstallStatusbar, add the missing `invoke` import from `@tauri-apps/api/core` to enable the Tauri command layer required for the bridge relays.\n\nFinally, in BakeExtensionManifest, prevent dev-mode hangs by writing only to `BundlePath` (skipping `DebugPath`) when no extensions are found. This ensures the empty stub in the `.app` bundle does not trigger a timeout in the live extension host during development, allowing it to fall back to a runtime scan safely.\n\nThese changes eliminate double-firing events, prevent memory leaks, fix SCM visibility issues, correct completion rendering, and stabilize the build process for empty extension environments.",
			"SHA": "1c848470a27833378b38c6651b381cc9ddfc417d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T07:05:43Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				155,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Sky): Support named-key payloads and register resolver for custom editors\n\nThe previous implementation in InstallWebview incorrectly assumed positional arguments for custom editor payloads. After the Cocoon extension host switched to named-key payloads (containing `viewType`, `options`, and `selector`), the editor failed to register custom editor capabilities because `Args[1]` was empty.\n\nUpdate the payload parsing logic to defensively handle both the new named-key format and the legacy positional format. Extract `viewType`, `options`, and `selector` from the primary payload fields, falling back to the `args` array only if necessary.\n\nAdditionally, register the custom editor with `IEditorResolverService` using a `priority.option` fallback. This ensures the VS Code activation event (`onCustomEditor:*`) fires correctly when manifest-based registration is delayed due to lazy extension activation. The resolver includes a safe `createEditorInput` implementation that defers to the builtin factory to prevent crashes if the resolver is invoked before the extension is fully ready.\n\nThese changes restore full functionality for custom editors (e.g., Markdown preview, image viewers) and ensure proper lifecycle management during extension activation.",
			"SHA": "2bda9da6327242388b0ffc821ce7d5cd2f383fa9"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T06:28:33Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				155,
				5
			],
			"Message": "fix(Sky): Prevent double-dispatch in bridge relays and fix Problems panel initialization\n\nRemove redundant SimpleRelay registrations in InstallDebug, InstallTasksAndDecorations, and InstallWebview that caused double-dispatch of events (e.g., `cel:debug:addBreakpoints`) by firing both the generic DOM relay and the specific service handler.\n\nIn InstallDiagnostics, refactor the bridge to resolve the \"count shows but panel empty\" issue by ensuring the Problems panel initializes correctly on every diagnostic batch, not just the first. This includes: (1) Throttling `ViewsSvc.openView` calls to 1Hz during rapid updates; (2) Reviving `relatedInformation` URI strings to objects so labels render correctly; (3) Persistently clearing the `activeFile` filter if it was previously set; and (4) Removing the one-shot guard to handle late-activating language servers like rust-analyzer.\n\nAdditionally, fix a memory leak in InstallEditorOperations by properly disposing of selection change listeners when the active editor switches, and correct the array mutation in InstallScm to use spread syntax for `splice` to avoid nested array insertion.\n\nThese changes ensure strict event routing, prevent unbounded listener accumulation, and guarantee diagnostic consistency across all file types and language server states.",
			"SHA": "f8b6900822907dcd4cb2be8fa336f9685966a70a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T06:03:40Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				155,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Sky): Force Problems panel initialization to sync early markers\n\nResolve the issue where diagnostic markers arrive before the Problems panel view is instantiated, causing a mismatch between the problem count in the status bar and the empty panel. The previous implementation failed to trigger `MarkersView.reInitialize()` because `getViewWithId` returned null if the `ViewPaneContainer` wasn't yet created.\n\nRefactor the one-time success path in `InstallDiagnostics.ts` to explicitly call `ViewsSvc.openView` with `false` to reveal the panel and force initialization without stealing focus. This ensures subscriptions activate and the view reflects the current marker state. Additionally, clear any persisted `activeFile` filter from the Memento that could otherwise hide markers when the view finally renders. Comprehensive logging via `MountainIPCInvoke` is added to track the first push state, filter stats, and initialization success or failure.",
			"SHA": "d6ea32bec4c1067b36608254022b3abf1e809044"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T05:33:52Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				155,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Integrate extension manifest baking and bundle compression\n\nIntroduce two new Astro integrations in Sky to optimize the build pipeline for the Rust/Tauri architecture. BakeExtensionManifest scans user and system extension directories at build time, resolves NLS localization strings, and generates a static JSON manifest for Mountain to consume at runtime, eliminating the need for dynamic scanning. CompressBundle applies Brotli compression to text-based assets in the final output, respecting modification timestamps to avoid redundant processing.\n\nBoth integrations are conditionally enabled in astro.config.ts based on the build mode. This reduces the runtime overhead for the editor startup and decreases the final application bundle size for distribution.",
			"SHA": "68df4ab4f20dabc5861fa23522397ddbefa22311"
		}
	],
